WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 1 Leader Video
Unit 1, Lesson 1: Apologetics

1
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.290
In 1 Peter 3.15, Peter wrote this,

2
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:14.290
But in your hearts, set apart Christ as Lord.

3
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.290
Always be prepared to give an answer to everyone who asks you,

4
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.290
to give a reason for the hope that you have.

5
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.290
But do this with gentleness and respect.

6
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.290
Oftentimes when we're talking about things like apologetics,

7
00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:34.290
this verse is sort of the foundational verse that everyone seems to cite.

8
00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:39.290
Why? Well, because in this verse is where we get the idea of apologetics.

9
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:43.290
So Peter is asking us or commanding us to give a reason.

10
00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.290
He's saying give an actual reason.

11
00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.290
Well, what does it mean to give a reason?

12
00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.290
Well, in this context, it means to give a defense.

13
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:59.290
Give some kind of defending idea of what it means about what you believe.

14
00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:05.290
This is actually the Greek word apologia.

15
00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.290
And that's where we get the idea of apologetics.

16
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.290
It literally comes from the word apology.

17
00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:15.290
Now we're not talking about I'm apologizing for what I believe.

18
00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.290
But if you can imagine for a moment a courtroom scenario

19
00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:22.290
where you were on the stand and you had to give sort of a defense,

20
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.290
you had to give a reason for your actions, a reason for what you believe,

21
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.290
or a reason just for what you're doing.

22
00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:33.290
Well, in the ancient world, in the context that Peter is talking about here

23
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:37.290
is to a bunch of Christians who are being persecuted by the Roman government.

24
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:43.290
Now here, Peter's telling the believers to be prepared,

25
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.290
to know why you believe what you believe,

26
00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.290
to be able to stand in a formal sense in this context

27
00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.290
to give a reason, to give a defense,

28
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:55.290
to defend one's belief in something.

29
00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.290
And we take this command that Peter gives the early Christians

30
00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:03.290
and we say, you know what, we have the exact same responsibility in our day.

31
00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.290
It's to be able to stand when the questions come

32
00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:10.290
and be able to give a reason for what we believe and why we believe it.

33
00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:13.290
So essentially this is what apologetics is

34
00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:18.290
and this is what your students are going to embark on this coming year.

35
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.290
But it's more than just making a defense.

36
00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.290
It's the idea that we are both called

37
00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.290
but we're also called to be capable.

38
00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:30.290
See, it's more than just saying, I have to give a defense.

39
00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.290
How are you going to give a defense?

40
00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.290
What do you know to be able to stand there

41
00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.290
and tell somebody what you believe and why?

42
00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.290
So this is exactly what we start to see

43
00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.290
and what your students are going to start to see

44
00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:48.290
with Peter in their early stages of acts, right?

45
00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.290
So if you look at what Peter says in acts,

46
00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:56.290
we've got this guy who literally at the crucifixion ran away

47
00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:02.290
but then all of a sudden in acts is proclaiming what he's seen and heard

48
00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.290
and we see in acts 420, Peter say,

49
00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:10.290
we can do nothing but speak of the things that we have seen and heard.

50
00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.290
So there are just this massive compelling nature of them

51
00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.290
to be able to speak about the things that they've seen and heard.

52
00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.290
Now it is important to remember

53
00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:24.290
that some people might not really think that this idea of apologetics

54
00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.290
is all that necessary.

55
00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:30.290
In fact, some might even say it's dangerous

56
00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.290
and they might even look to passages like 1 Corinthians chapter 2

57
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.290
where Paul gives this idea that it's not by human wisdom

58
00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:43.290
or human power that he comes to the Corinthian church.

59
00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.290
That he didn't come with wise and persuasive words

60
00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.290
and a lot of people will take this to mean that we don't argue

61
00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.290
and we don't want to persuade people

62
00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:57.290
but in the context that's not exactly what Paul is talking about.

63
00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.290
So we are called to maturity.

64
00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.290
We're called to be able to give evidence.

65
00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.290
We'll see throughout this study if you look at the life of Jesus,

66
00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.290
you'll look at the life of Paul, you'll look at the things that Peter did,

67
00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:15.290
all of them gave consistent and good reasons

68
00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.290
for what they believed and why they believed it.

69
00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.290
So what we're really asking students right out of the gate here

70
00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.290
is to consider that very question.

71
00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:25.290
Why do you believe what you believe

72
00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.290
and can you discuss those beliefs intelligently?

73
00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.290
Why do you believe what you believe?

74
00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:36.290
So you and your students are headed on a huge, huge journey here.

75
00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:40.290
And it starts with getting students to start thinking

76
00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.290
about these kinds of spiritual conversations.

77
00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.290
Some of the stuff that we're going to be talking about

78
00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.290
is some pretty heavy stuff.

79
00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.290
Some of the topics that we're going to be dealing with

80
00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.290
are going to be very challenging not only for you

81
00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.290
but challenging for your students as well.

82
00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:58.290
So you want to create a certain kind of environment.

83
00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.290
Now some of you may already have this environment in your groups

84
00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.290
and some of you may not

85
00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.290
but I want to encourage you to create an environment

86
00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.290
that really fosters this key idea

87
00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.290
of being able to ask and answer questions.

88
00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.290
Now this might seem really, really simple.

89
00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.290
Like well yeah, of course my students can ask questions

90
00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.290
but you would be surprised that the number of students

91
00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:25.290
that just don't feel like they can ask any question.

92
00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.290
Not just the difficult question

93
00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:32.290
but maybe the question that just really questions their own faith.

94
00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:36.290
That really sort of invites in this idea of doubt.

95
00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.290
Now we're going to be dealing with doubt but much later.

96
00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.290
So you have to be able to create an environment

97
00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:45.290
where your students feel like they can ask anything.

98
00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:49.290
Where they feel welcome where it's a safe place.

99
00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:53.290
But that doesn't mean that you have to have all of the answers.

100
00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.290
Because let's be honest, you're not going to have all the answers.

101
00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.290
Your students ask great questions.

102
00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.290
In all the years that I've been a Christian educator

103
00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.290
I have seen some amazing questions

104
00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:07.290
that you just sort of stand there with your jaw drop.

105
00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.290
I don't know what to say to that

106
00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.290
because I never would have thought of that question

107
00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.290
and I love those kinds of questions.

108
00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:18.290
Don't feel like you have to have all the answers.

109
00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.290
But what goes even further than having all of the answers

110
00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.290
is being able to walk alongside of a student and say

111
00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.290
hey listen, I don't know the answer

112
00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:31.290
but let's you and me figure this out together.

113
00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.290
That's going to do exactly what our goal is.

114
00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.290
That's going to create a stronger relationship

115
00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.290
between you and your students.

116
00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:42.290
As well as at the same time figuring out the answer to their question.

117
00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:46.290
So use the resources that you have available to you

118
00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.290
inside your church.

119
00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:53.290
Possibly a school or a seminary that might be nearby.

120
00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.290
Friends and family of yours that may have a deeper understanding.

121
00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.290
But also use us.

122
00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:01.290
We're here at awanowym.org

123
00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:05.290
We have a ton of resources in a library that we are continuing to build.

124
00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:09.290
Definitely check out Sean's website at SeanMcDowell.org

125
00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:13.290
He's got a ton of resources and if you still are stumped

126
00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.290
you can even contact us directly

127
00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:18.290
and we are happy to help you in any way that we can.

128
00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.290
We are here to assist you in this journey

129
00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.290
but I can't stress enough.

130
00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.290
Be sure that your small group leaders

131
00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:29.290
and you in terms of a large group, whatever it is

132
00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.290
that you have going on

133
00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:35.290
make sure your students feel like they can do this.

134
00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:38.290
That they can ask anything.

135
00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:42.290
And it might start with you giving them some of the questions

136
00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:47.290
that even you have in terms of figuring out what this looks like.

137
00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:50.290
So get ready, dive in, don't hold back

138
00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:54.290
and know that all of us here at the Home Office are praying for you.

139
00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.290
Praying for each other and other groups around the country

140
00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:00.290
that are on this journey with you.

141
00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:04.290
As we navigate together what this looks like

142
00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:08.290
as we explore deeper of what it means to be believers in Christ

143
00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:11.290
what that looks like, how do we defend it

144
00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.290
and how do we guide our students so that when they graduate

145
00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.290
when they move on to bigger and better things beyond your youth group

146
00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:22.290
they are prepared to successfully engage their culture

147
00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.290
and further the Kingdom of God.

